     1	# Model lifecycle
     2	
     3	The plugin schedules requests while a model adapter retains TT programs,
     4	traces, KV storage, and possibly per-request device state. The model adapter
     5	must prepare execution before serving, preserve request ownership when batch
     6	rows move, and release persistent captures while the mesh remains open.
     7	See the [interface guide](MODEL_INTERFACE.md) for setup and execution calls.
     8	
     9	## Warmup and trace capture
    10	
    11	`TTWorker.compile_or_warm_up_model` runs `TTModelRunner.warmup_model` when
    12	`tt.enable_model_warmup` is true, which is the default. The adapter supplies:
    13	
    14	```python
    15	warmup_model_prefill(kv_cache=..., can_sample_on_device=..., enable_trace=...)
    16	warmup_model_decode(kv_cache=..., max_batch_size=..., num_blocks=...,
    17	                    can_sample_on_device=..., enable_trace=...)
    18	```
    19	
    20	`max_batch_size` is the merged TT batch capacity. `num_blocks` is the profiled
    21	maximum block-table width per request. When effective device grammar support
    22	is enabled, decode warmup also receives `can_sample_device_grammar=True`.
    23	
    24	1. `TTModelRunner.warmup_model` calls `warmup_model_prefill` and then
    25	   `warmup_model_decode` with `enable_trace=False`.
    26	2. `TTModelRunner.warmup_model` resets `already_warmed_up_prefill=False` if
    27	   the adapter exposes `already_warmed_up_prefill`.
    28	3. For `tt.trace_mode="all"`, `TTModelRunner.warmup_model` calls
    29	   `warmup_model_prefill(enable_trace=True)`.
    30	4. For `tt.trace_mode="all"` or `"decode_only"`,
    31	   `TTModelRunner.warmup_model` calls `warmup_model_decode(enable_trace=True)`.
    32	
    33	The adapter must prepare the operators and persistent buffers that traced
    34	execution uses. Eager warmup must cover traced operators, and prefill warmup
    35	must cover supported sequence lengths. Compilation or incompatible buffer
    36	allocation after trace capture can invalidate retained trace storage.
    37	`tt.trace_mode="none"` skips trace capture but still runs enabled eager warmup.
    38	
    39	Source: `TTModelRunner.warmup_model` in
    40	[model_runner.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_runner.py).
    41	
    42	## Request state
    43	
    44	Device-state slots identify adapter-owned request state. A prefill row is not
    45	necessarily the slot that owns that request. KV page addresses and state slots
    46	serve different purposes; the adapter must honor both.
    47	
    48	| Interface | Adapter responsibility |
    49	|---|---|
    50	| `prefill_forward(empty_slots=[...])` | Write each prefill row's state into the corresponding destination slot; preserve live state in other slots. Stateless adapters can ignore `empty_slots`. |
    51	| `decode_forward(slot_remap=...)` | Gather old state so destination slot `i` reads old slot `slot_remap[i]` before decode uses that state. `None` means identity. Apply the whole permutation without overwriting state still needed by another destination. |
    52	| `note_state_slots_moved(moves)` | Optional front-packed execution callback receiving `{old_slot: new_slot}` after the plugin commits a movement. Update adapter-owned session identities; do not repeat a device gather already performed by `decode_forward`. |
    53	| `release_request(slot)` | Optional front-packed execution callback that releases the state of the request currently owning `slot`. The plugin passes the current slot, not necessarily the original prefill slot. |
    54	
    55	`TTModelRunner._decode_state_slot_remap` covers the full state-slot capacity,
    56	which can exceed a bucketed decode's token row count. The adapter must preserve
    57	off-batch state moved by that permutation. `TTModelRunner` commits the new
    58	ownership only after `decode_forward` accepts the submission, then calls
    59	`note_state_slots_moved` when applicable.
    60	
    61	In front-packed execution, `TTModelRunner._update_states` calls
    62	`release_request` for finished and preempted requests while slot ownership is
    63	available. A resumed request rebuilds state through prefill.
    64	A request omitted from a prefill-only step can still own live decode state;
    65	absence from one submitted batch does not authorize the adapter to release
    66	that request's state.
    67	
    68	Lane-DP uses scheduler-owned stable slots. `TTLaneInputBatch.apply_step_plan`
    69	removes finished and preempted requests without calling `release_request`;
    70	the lane path also does not issue `note_state_slots_moved` callbacks. A model
    71	adapter that requires those callbacks cannot assume lane-DP supplies them.
    72	
    73	Block-output models must implement callable `release_request` and
    74	`release_persistent_capture`. Adaptive block-output models with
    75	`max_num_seqs > 1` must also implement `note_state_slots_moved`.
    76	Stateful speculative adapters have additional ownership duties in the
    77	[speculative contract](SPEC_DECODE_CONTRACT.md).
    78	
    79	### Stage inputs
    80	
    81	A model that declares `supports_stage_inputs` receives each request's payload
    82	on prefill only, as a read-only snapshot without the request ID. So:
    83	
    84	- Decode-time state derived from the payload is the model's to keep, in its
    85	  slot-owned state, written by the request's last prefill chunk.
    86	- Work derived from the payload, such as a speaker embedding, cannot be cached
    87	  across prefill chunks by slot: a request's row and slot can change between
    88	  chunks.
    89	- `warmup_model_prefill` receives no `stage_inputs`. A model whose prefill is
    90	  built from the payload supplies its own warmup payload.
    91	
    92	Sources: `_alloc_prefill_state_slots`, `_decode_state_slot_remap`,
    93	`_release_model_request`, and `_update_states` in
    94	[model_runner.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_runner.py);
    95	`TTLaneInputBatch.apply_step_plan` in
    96	[input_batch.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/input_batch.py).
    97	
    98	## Shutdown
    99	
   100	1. `TTWorker.shutdown` calls `TTModelRunner.shutdown` while the mesh is open.
   101	2. `TTModelRunner.shutdown` calls optional `release_persistent_capture()` once
   102	   to release model-lifetime captures. The adapter must release device
   103	   resources that require an open mesh here. The runner logs exceptions and
   104	   marks capture release complete rather than retrying capture release.
   105	3. `TTWorker.shutdown` closes the mesh.
   106	
   107	The plugin does not call a generic model `shutdown()` hook or guarantee model
   108	destruction before mesh close. Keep device-dependent capture cleanup in
   109	`release_persistent_capture`.
   110	
   111	Sources: `TTModelRunner.shutdown` in
   112	[model_runner.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_runner.py) and
   113	`TTWorker.shutdown` in [worker.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/worker.py).

