     1	# Model setup and KV storage
     2	
     3	The TT plugin selects a model class, opens a device mesh, constructs a model
     4	instance, and asks the model instance to allocate KV storage. This guide calls
     5	the model class implementation an **adapter**. The adapter supplies TT model
     6	execution; the plugin supplies vLLM scheduling and translates vLLM cache plans.
     7	Start with the [interface overview](MODEL_INTERFACE.md) for the full lifecycle.
     8	
     9	## Registration and class declarations
    10	
    11	`--model` identifies the checkpoint. The checkpoint's `hf_config.architectures`
    12	selects the adapter through vLLM's model registry. Registration uses a lazy
    13	`module.path:ClassName` target. `TTPlatform.check_and_update_config` adds a `TT`
    14	prefix to checkpoint architecture names before resolving the TT adapter.
    15	The adapter module must be importable in each vLLM process that resolves it.
    16	
    17	Registration precedence is `TT_MODEL_CLASS_OVERRIDES`, then `EXTRA_MODELS_DIR`,
    18	then built-in registrations. Use the README examples for
    19	[bundle registration](../README.md#registering-models-dynamically-extra_models_dir)
    20	and [class selection](../README.md#selecting-a-serving-class-tt_model_class_overrides).
    21	`TT_VLLM_BUILTIN_MODELS=0` disables ordinary built-in registrations;
    22	DiffusionGemma aliases remain registered.
    23	
    24	Declare `model_capabilities` on the adapter class so
    25	`TTPlatform.check_and_update_config` can read support before construction.
    26	Keep class and instance declarations consistent because runtime consumers also
    27	read `model_capabilities`. See [Model capabilities](MODEL_CAPABILITIES.md) for
    28	every supported key, default, and validation rule. Operators request supported
    29	behavior through vLLM arguments and `additional_config["tt"]`.
    30	
    31	Sources: `register_tt_models`, `_register_models_from_extra_dir`, and
    32	`TTPlatform.check_and_update_config` in [platform.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/platform.py).
    33	
    34	## Construction and mesh ownership
    35	
    36	1. `TTWorker.init_device` binds visible devices and repeats platform validation
    37	   in the worker process.
    38	2. `TTWorker.init_device` opens a `ttnn.MeshDevice`. `set_fabric` applies hardware
    39	   defaults, `model_capabilities["fabric_config"]`, then explicit launch
    40	   overrides. `set_fabric` does nothing for a single-device mesh.
    41	3. `TTWorker.init_device` computes the KV block budget and fits block-output
    42	   `max_model_len` before model construction.
    43	4. `TTModelLoader.load_model` calls the required class-callable factory:
    44	
    45	```python
    46	adapter = model_class.initialize_vllm_model(
    47	    model_config.hf_config,
    48	    device_config.device,
    49	    max_batch_size,
    50	    max_seq_len=model_config.max_model_len,
    51	    tt_data_parallel=tt_data_parallel,
    52	    optimizations=optimizations,
    53	)
    54	```
    55	
    56	`initialize_vllm_model` returns the instance that implements the execution,
    57	allocation, and lifecycle hooks. The adapter owns model and weight preparation;
    58	`TTModelLoader.download_model` and `TTModelLoader.load_weights` are not implemented.
    59	
    60	| Factory input | Meaning |
    61	|---|---|
    62	| `model_config.hf_config` | Hugging Face checkpoint configuration. |
    63	| `device_config.device` | Already-open `ttnn.MeshDevice`; `TTWorker` owns mesh closure. |
    64	| `max_batch_size` | Engine-local capacity, including all lanes in lane-DP. |
    65	| `max_seq_len` | Resolved `model_config.max_model_len`. |
    66	| `tt_data_parallel` | In-process lane count; 1 for each standard multi-process DP rank. |
    67	| `optimizations` | `None`, `"performance"`, or `"accuracy"`, from `additional_config["tt"]`. |
    68	
    69	`TTWorker.shutdown` releases runner resources before closing the mesh. See
    70	[Model lifecycle](MODEL_LIFECYCLE.md) for adapter cleanup hooks.
    71	
    72	Sources: [loader.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/loader.py), `TTWorker.init_device` and
    73	`set_fabric` in [worker.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/worker.py), and
    74	`get_tt_max_batch_size` / `get_tt_data_parallel_size` in [config.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/config.py).
    75	
    76	## KV budget and specifications
    77	
    78	The optional class-callable `get_max_tokens_all_users` supplies the KV token
    79	capacity for one lane or one standard-DP rank, before plugin-added headroom:
    80	
    81	```python
    82	model_class.get_max_tokens_all_users(
    83	    model_name=model_config.model,
    84	    num_devices=num_devices,
    85	    tt_data_parallel=tt_data_parallel,
    86	    max_model_len=model_config.max_model_len,
    87	    max_num_seqs=per_lane_max_num_seqs,
    88	)
    89	```
    90	
    91	`num_devices` counts physical devices in the worker's open mesh.
    92	`max_num_seqs` is the per-lane or per-rank capacity, unlike the merged capacity
    93	passed to `initialize_vllm_model`. The plugin uses `131_072` when the sizing
    94	call raises `AttributeError`, including when `get_max_tokens_all_users` is absent.
    95	The plugin adds output reservation and applicable sliding-window headroom.
    96	The plugin does not measure free device memory to choose this KV budget.
    97	
    98	The optional class-callable `get_kv_cache_spec(vllm_config)` returns
    99	`dict[str, KVCacheSpec] | None`. `TTWorker.get_kv_cache_spec` uses a homogeneous
   100	specification named `"foo"` when `get_kv_cache_spec` is absent or returns `None`.
   101	For per-layer specifications, use names containing `layers.<index>`, such as
   102	`model.layers.5.self_attn`, and cover every attention-layer index.
   103	
   104	`TTModelRunner` accepts `AttentionSpec` groups and `UniformTypeKVCacheSpecs`
   105	groups. `UniformTypeKVCacheSpecs` can carry different per-layer shapes within
   106	one group. The worker advertises only the vLLM `LBNHC` cache layout.
   107	
   108	A stage with no token KV cache, such as an audio decoder, uses a `TTWorker`
   109	subclass that sets `uses_token_kv_cache = False`. That worker sizes no KV pool
   110	and reports an empty KV specification. vLLM then treats the stage as
   111	attention-free: it skips `determine_available_memory`, which returns `0`, and
   112	passes the runner a KV cache config with no groups. `TTModelRunner` refuses
   113	that config, so the subclass also names a runner, in `model_runner_cls`, that
   114	accepts it.
   115	
   116	Sources: `get_num_available_blocks_tt`, `TTWorker.get_kv_cache_spec`, and
   117	`TTWorker.determine_available_memory` in [worker.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/worker.py).
   118	
   119	## Allocation and page-table routing
   120	
   121	1. `TTModelRunner._build_per_layer_specs` translates the vLLM cache plan into
   122	   `(shape, dtype, tensor_idx)` triples, ordered by attention-layer index.
   123	2. `TTModelRunner._allocate_kv_caches` calls the instance's
   124	   `allocate_kv_cache_per_layer(per_layer_specs)` when the adapter exposes it.
   125	   Otherwise, `TTModelRunner._allocate_kv_caches` calls
   126	   `allocate_kv_cache(shape, dtype, num_layers)` and requires identical per-layer
   127	   shapes and dtypes.
   128	3. `TTModelRunner` stores the allocator result as `kv_caches` and passes the
   129	   allocator result to warmup and execution as `kv_cache`.
   130	
   131	`shape` is `(num_blocks, heads_per_device, block_size, head_size)`, where
   132	`heads_per_device = spec.num_kv_heads // min(devices_per_lane, spec.num_kv_heads)`
   133	and `devices_per_lane = num_devices // tt_data_parallel`.
   134	`tensor_idx` identifies shared storage: layers with the same `tensor_idx` share
   135	a buffer. A single-group cache gives every attention layer a separate
   136	`tensor_idx`. The plugin treats the allocator result as opaque model storage.
   137	
   138	When vLLM creates multiple KV groups, `TTModelRunner` expands group page tables
   139	into `page_tables_per_layer`, ordered by attention-layer index. Prefill and
   140	decode receive `page_tables_per_layer` in addition to group 0's `page_table`.
   141	Each per-layer tensor has shape
   142	`[tt_max_batch_size, max_num_blocks_per_req]`, with unused rows and columns
   143	zero-padded. The per-layer row capacity can exceed `tokens.shape[0]` during
   144	prefill or bucketed decode.
   145	A single-group cache omits `page_tables_per_layer`, including a single group
   146	with heterogeneous per-layer shapes. See [Model execution](MODEL_EXECUTION.md).
   147	
   148	For sliding-window groups, the class attribute
   149	`_HYBRID_KV_CACHE_GROUPS_ENABLED=True` enables additional sizing headroom when
   150	the checkpoint supplies `sliding_window`. The adapter must implement the
   151	addressing required by its cache specifications. For a speculative drafter
   152	that shares bounded target storage, the adapter must also preserve the target
   153	and drafter addressing requirements in [the speculative contract](SPEC_DECODE_CONTRACT.md).
   154	
   155	Sources: `_kv_cache_shape`, `_build_per_layer_specs`, `_block_tables_per_layer`,
   156	and `submit_prefill` in [model_runner.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_runner.py);
   157	`submit_decode` in [async_decode.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/async_decode.py).

