     1	# Model execution
     2	
     3	`TTModelRunner` translates scheduled vLLM requests into model adapter calls.
     4	The model adapter executes prefill or decode and returns logits or sampled
     5	tokens in the submitted row order. The plugin selects sampling for the whole
     6	submitted batch and applies the resulting tokens to vLLM request state.
     7	Start with the [interface guide](MODEL_INTERFACE.md) for setup and lifecycle.
     8	The plugin rejects encoder-decoder models and `prompt_embeds` input.
     9	
    10	## Rows, positions, and page tables
    11	
    12	`B` below means the number of submitted tensor rows, including decode padding.
    13	`V` means vocabulary width. These are notation for this page, not API names.
    14	
    15	- Ordinary execution packs active request rows at the front. Decode may pad
    16	  to the configured capacity or the nearest `tt_supported_decode_batch_sizes`
    17	  value that fits. Publish only batch sizes prepared on the loaded instance.
    18	- Lane-DP prefill packs only scheduled requests. Lane-DP decode uses merged
    19	  stable slots, so inactive rows can occur between active rows. Standard
    20	  multi-process DP gives each worker an independent model and batch.
    21	- `start_pos=-1` marks an inactive decode row. The model adapter must not
    22	  interpret an inactive row as a live request or modify another request's state.
    23	- `page_table` is the first KV group's integer logical-to-physical block
    24	  table. If the resolved cache has multiple groups, the plugin also sends
    25	  `page_tables_per_layer`, ordered by attention-layer index. The model adapter
    26	  must use the page table for each layer. See [KV setup](MODEL_SETUP.md).
    27	
    28	`TTModelInput` is an internal plugin payload. The model adapter receives the
    29	keyword arguments below, not a `TTModelInput` object. Source:
    30	[model_input.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_input.py),
    31	`TTModelRunner._prepare_model_inputs` in
    32	[model_runner.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_runner.py), and
    33	`TTLaneInputBatch` in [input_batch.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/input_batch.py).
    34	
    35	## Prefill
    36	
    37	`TTModelRunner.submit_prefill` calls `prefill_forward` with these keywords:
    38	
    39	| Keyword | Meaning |
    40	|---|---|
    41	| `tokens` | CPU integer tensor `[B, T]`, containing token history from position 0 through the largest scheduled chunk end. |
    42	| `start_pos` | One absolute chunk start per row. Front-packed prefill supplies a NumPy array; lane-DP supplies a torch tensor. |
    43	| `prompt_lens` | One exclusive chunk end per row, supplied as a NumPy array. `prompt_lens[i]` is not the chunk length. |
    44	| `page_table`, `kv_cache` | Block addresses and the object returned by the adapter's KV allocator. |
    45	| `enable_trace` | True when `tt.trace_mode="all"`. |
    46	| `empty_slots` | When supplied, one destination device-state slot per submitted row. Preserve state belonging to other slots. |
    47	| `page_tables_per_layer` | Supplied for multiple KV groups, as described above. |
    48	| `sampling_params` | Supplied only when this prefill uses device sampling. See the sampling section. |
    49	| `stage_inputs` | Supplied only when the model declares `supports_stage_inputs`. One entry per row: the request's stage payload as a plain dict, or `None`. The same payload arrives with every prefill of a request, so a chunked or resumed prefill sees it again. Decode receives none; see [stage inputs](MODEL_LIFECYCLE.md#stage-inputs). |
    50	
    51	For row `i`, `prefill_forward` computes
    52	`tokens[i, start_pos[i]:prompt_lens[i]]`. For example, `start_pos[i]=128` and
    53	`prompt_lens[i]=192` request 64 tokens while retaining absolute positions.
    54	Prefix-cache hits and resumed requests can also have nonzero `start_pos`.
    55	Resume prefill can replay generated tokens to rebuild KV state.
    56	
    57	The model adapter returns host logits `[B, 1, V]` for host sampling, or sampled
    58	token IDs for device sampling. The plugin has no separate prefill readback
    59	hook. `TTModelRunner` suppresses output for intermediate prefill chunks and
    60	selects host sampling when a submitted prefill contains intermediate chunks,
    61	so intermediate chunks must not advance a device sampler.
    62	
    63	### Multimodal inputs and request-specific RoPE
    64	
    65	For multimodal prefill, `_gather_multi_modal_inputs` forwards every field the
    66	model's multimodal processor put on an item under its own name: `pixel_values`
    67	and `image_grid_thw` are always present (as `None` entries when a processor
    68	does not emit them), and any further field is forwarded without the runner
    69	knowing the model's contract (for example `pixel_position_ids`,
    70	`pixel_values_videos` / `pixel_position_ids_videos` for video and
    71	`input_features` / `input_features_mask` for audio). Image, video and audio
    72	items are accepted; any other item kind raises `NotImplementedError`.
    73	
    74	The return value is a dict keyed by field name. Each value is a list in
    75	submitted request order (the persistent batch order the model input tensors
    76	use). A text-only request has `None`; a request with items has a list in
    77	that request's multimodal-item order, one entry per item. An item whose
    78	payload is absent (a prefix-cached item arrives with its tensors stripped) or
    79	that lacks the field contributes `None` for that field.
    80	
    81	Two integer metadata fields are appended after the processor fields, so
    82	positional readers of the processor fields are unchanged:
    83	`mm_placeholder_offsets` and `mm_placeholder_lengths`. Both are in absolute
    84	prompt-token coordinates: the offset is the index of the item's first
    85	placeholder token in the request's prompt and the length is its placeholder
    86	count, so a model that prefills in chunks can tell which items the current
    87	chunk covers (an item whose placeholders lie past the chunk end has no slots
    88	yet). They are `None` when the item carries no placeholder position.
    89	
    90	When `model_config.uses_mrope` enables request-specific RoPE, `prefill_forward`
    91	returns `(output, rope_deltas)`, with one delta per request. On decode,
    92	`TTAsyncDecodeController` supplies `rope_deltas_all_users` after a layout
    93	change or a new request, and `None` otherwise. Lane-DP rejects
    94	request-specific RoPE.
    95	
    96	## Decode
    97	
    98	`TTAsyncDecodeController.submit_decode` calls `decode_forward` with:
    99	
   100	| Keyword | Meaning |
   101	|---|---|
   102	| `tokens` | CPU integer tensor `[B, 1]` for ordinary decode. |
   103	| `start_pos` | CPU integer tensor `[B]` of absolute positions; inactive rows contain `-1`. |
   104	| `page_table`, `kv_cache` | Block addresses and adapter-owned KV storage. |
   105	| `enable_trace` | True for `tt.trace_mode="all"` or `"decode_only"`. |
   106	| `read_from_device` | `False` for front-packed and asynchronous decode. Synchronous lane-DP requests `True`, except for deferred grammar sampling or selective readback. The adapter must support the readback mode its execution path requests. |
   107	| `page_tables_per_layer` | Supplied for multiple KV groups. |
   108	| `slot_remap` | When present, destination slot `i` reads previous slot `slot_remap[i]`. Supplied for both host and device sampling. See [state ownership](MODEL_LIFECYCLE.md#request-state). |
   109	| `sampling_params` | Supplied for immediate device sampling; absent for host sampling and deferred grammar sampling. |
   110	| `prompt_tokens`, `output_tokens` | Supplied together when device sampling needs token history for penalties. Histories use `-1` padding. |
   111	
   112	The [decode reload contract](DECODE_RELOAD_CONTRACT.md) specifies
   113	`decode_input_update_contract`, `reload_inputs`, `reload_page_table`,
   114	`reload_sampling_params`, and `reset_sampling_state`, plus the version-0
   115	`reset_batch` call. The model adapter must execute the negotiated update
   116	commands even when host token tensors lag resident device state.
   117	
   118	The [speculative contract](SPEC_DECODE_CONTRACT.md) defines wide verification
   119	inputs, `num_valid_drafts`, `accepted_counts`, `spec_mode`, `VerifyOutput`, and
   120	`propose_draft_tokens`. An ordinary decode receives no `spec_mode` and must
   121	not return `VerifyOutput`.
   122	
   123	### Stage outputs
   124	
   125	A model that declares `supports_stage_outputs` implements
   126	`pop_stage_outputs()`. `submit_decode` calls it right after every
   127	`decode_forward` and keeps the result with that submission.
   128	
   129	- Return one entry per decode row: the stage frame this forward completed
   130	  for the row's request, or `None`. Padding rows must be `None`.
   131	- The call comes before any device synchronization, and the plugin never
   132	  synchronizes or reads a stage frame's `data`. `data` must be host-resident,
   133	  picklable, and own its storage until the consumer reads it. Reading from
   134	  the device inside `pop_stage_outputs()` is allowed; it blocks the step.
   135	- The runner tags each stage frame `(request ID, frame_index)`.
   136	  `frame_index` is the row's decode position minus the request's prompt
   137	  length: the step that consumes output token `k` completes stage frame `k`.
   138	- The stage frames are published on the step's `ModelRunnerOutput`. Read
   139	  them with `stage_outputs.get_tt_stage_outputs`.
   140	- Scheduling is synchronous for these models: they cannot declare
   141	  `supports_async_decode`, without which the platform turns async
   142	  scheduling off.
   143	- Prefill completes no stage frame, and the runner never calls the hook for
   144	  it.
   145	
   146	A stage model's request cannot be preempted and resumed: a resume re-prefills
   147	from the token history, which does not hold the stage frames already emitted.
   148	The platform therefore requires `max_num_seqs=1`, refuses a forced
   149	prefix-cache reset while such a request runs (or aborts it first when the
   150	engine can tell its client), and `TTModelRunner` raises if a preemption
   151	reaches it anyway.
   152	
   153	## Decode readback and output conversion
   154	
   155	1. `TTAsyncDecodeController` calls `decode_forward`. The model adapter may
   156	   return a host torch tensor or an adapter-specific output object.
   157	2. For asynchronous readback, `TTAsyncDecodeController` calls
   158	   `read_decode_output(output, async_read=True)` when the adapter exposes
   159	   `read_decode_output`. The adapter returns `(output_handles, read_events)`.
   160	   Without `read_decode_output`, `decode_forward` must already return host
   161	   torch output. Keep asynchronous output buffers valid until consumption.
   162	3. `TTAsyncDecodeController.finalize_decode` synchronizes each TTNN read event.
   163	   For output that is not already host torch output, the controller calls
   164	   `process_decode_output_host(output_handles, is_tokens=perform_device_sampling)`.
   165	   The adapter returns host logits or sampled IDs. Synchronous decode uses
   166	   this conversion too when `decode_forward` returns adapter-specific output.
   167	4. `TTModelRunner` uses the last position in host logits `[B, S, V]`, commonly
   168	   `[B, 1, V]`, for sampling, or consumes device-sampled IDs `[B, 1]`.
   169	   For `output_tokens_per_step > 1`, the adapter returns
   170	   `[B, output_tokens_per_step]`; adaptive block
   171	   execution also permits one-token prefill and batched decode outputs.
   172	
   173	Here `S` is the returned sequence dimension; the front-packed sampler uses
   174	only position `S - 1`. Lane-DP host extraction also accepts `[B, V]` logits.
   175	
   176	For device logprobs, the adapter returns `(token_ids, logprobs)` through the
   177	same prefill or decode output boundary. `build_device_logprobs` accepts sampled
   178	logprobs or `(topk_logprobs, topk_indices)` according to the selected model's
   179	support. Exact payload handling is in
   180	[logprobs.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/logprobs.py).
   181	
   182	The optional `supports_compact_host_logits` and
   183	`supports_selective_host_readback` declarations allow scheduled-row host
   184	output in lane-DP. The [selective-read contract](DECODE_RELOAD_CONTRACT.md#host-sampling-output-and-selective-reads)
   185	defines `sample_rows`, output order, buffer ownership, and the two readback
   186	callbacks. Full-row output remains required when the plugin omits `sample_rows`.
   187	
   188	## Sampling and device grammar
   189	
   190	`sampling_params` is a `TTSamplingParams` object whose device-facing fields
   191	contain per-row Python lists: `temperature`, `top_k`, `top_p`,
   192	`presence_penalty`, `frequency_penalty`, `repetition_penalty`, `seed`,
   193	`num_logprobs`, and `enable_log_probs`. The plugin converts unspecified seeds
   194	to `None` and pads decode sampling rows with neutral defaults.
   195	
   196	`supports_sample_on_device` permits device sampling; the declaration does not
   197	force device sampling. `TTModelRunner.check_perform_device_sampling` selects
   198	one sampling path for the submitted batch. Ordinary adapters must return
   199	logits when the plugin selects host sampling, including for unsupported
   200	device controls. The [capability reference](MODEL_CAPABILITIES.md#sampling-and-async-capabilities)
   201	lists admission and fallback rules. Block-output requests have separate
   202	restrictions because host sampling cannot construct a multi-token block.
   203	
   204	For an eligible structured decode:
   205	
   206	1. `TTModelRunner.load_model` calls optional `enable_device_grammar()` and
   207	   requires `device_grammar_enabled=True` plus callable `sample_deferred_decode`.
   208	2. `TTAsyncDecodeController` calls `decode_forward(defer_device_sampling=True,
   209	   read_from_device=False, ...)` without `sampling_params`. The adapter retains
   210	   device logits without advancing the sampler.
   211	3. After vLLM supplies the grammar, `TTAsyncDecodeController` calls
   212	   `sample_deferred_decode(output, sampling_params=..., grammar_bitmask=...)`.
   213	   The adapter applies the packed int32 grammar mask and returns sampled
   214	   output through the ordinary decode conversion path.
   215	
   216	Each bit in `grammar_bitmask` names one vocabulary token; a one bit permits
   217	that token. The model adapter must apply the submitted row order.
   218	
   219	Structured prefill uses host sampling. Deferred grammar sampling requires
   220	synchronous scheduling and effective runtime support. A missing mask or a
   221	failure after deferred submission invalidates the runner's grammar path;
   222	the plugin raises instead of resampling an already advanced step on the host.
   223	
   224	Sources: `submit_prefill`, `check_perform_device_sampling`, and
   225	`_get_output_tokens` in [model_runner.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_runner.py);
   226	`submit_decode`, `finalize_decode`, and `complete_deferred_device_sampling` in
   227	[async_decode.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/async_decode.py).
   228	
   229	## Adapter sketches: DP=1 and lane-DP
   230	
   231	The sketches below are pseudocode. They show how an adapter maps submitted
   232	rows to KV storage and device state in the two single-process layouts. They
   233	omit tracing, device sampling, readback options, multimodal inputs, and
   234	`page_tables_per_layer`. Helper names such as `run_prefill`, `run_decode`, and
   235	`split_mesh` are adapter-internal, not plugin API.
   236	
   237	### DP=1 (front-packed)
   238	
   239	`tt_data_parallel` is 1. One KV cache serves all rows. Prefill row `i` uses
   240	`page_table[i]` and writes its device state to `empty_slots[i]`, which need
   241	not equal `i`. Decode padding rows have `start_pos=-1`.
   242	
   243	```python
   244	class MyModel:
   245	    @classmethod
   246	    def initialize_vllm_model(cls, hf_config, mesh_device, max_batch_size,
   247	                              max_seq_len, tt_data_parallel=1,
   248	                              optimizations=None):
   249	        assert tt_data_parallel == 1
   250	        return cls(hf_config, mesh_device, max_batch_size, max_seq_len)
   251	
   252	    def allocate_kv_cache(self, shape, dtype, num_layers):
   253	        # shape = (num_blocks, heads_per_device, block_size, head_size)
   254	        return [alloc_kv(self.mesh, shape, dtype) for _ in range(num_layers)]
   255	
   256	    def prefill_forward(self, tokens, start_pos, prompt_lens, page_table,
   257	                        kv_cache, empty_slots, **kwargs):
   258	        logits = []
   259	        for i in range(tokens.shape[0]):
   260	            chunk = tokens[i, start_pos[i]:prompt_lens[i]]

