    80	## Sampling and async capabilities
    81	
    82	| `model_capabilities` key | Default when absent | Meaning and current validation |
    83	|---|---|---|
    84	| `supports_sample_on_device` | `False` | Permits the requested `sample_on_device_mode`. The platform rejects any non-`None` sampling mode when this declaration is false. Runtime sampling requirements can still select host sampling. |
    85	| `max_device_top_k` | `None` | Bounds stochastic device sampling. `TTModelRunner.check_perform_device_sampling` selects host sampling when any selected sampling row has nonzero temperature and `top_k < 1` or `top_k > max_device_top_k`. Greedy rows do not trigger this restriction. The platform rejects any non-`None` value on a block-output model. The plugin does not otherwise validate the numeric type or range of `max_device_top_k`; model authors must supply the actual supported bound. |
    86	| `supports_device_penalties` | `True` | Permits device sampling with active penalties. When this declaration is false and `InputBatch.no_penalties` is false, `TTModelRunner.check_perform_device_sampling` selects host sampling. The default preserves the existing behavior of model implementations that predate this declaration. |
    87	| `supports_device_grammar` | `False` | Declares that decode sampling accepts vLLM's packed grammar bitmask after forward. The platform rejects a non-boolean value, a `True` value without `supports_sample_on_device`, and a `True` value on a block-output model. `TTModelRunner` keeps host grammar sampling without a `sample_on_device_mode`, with async scheduling, when tracing without model warmup, or when the loaded model has no compatible sampler. Structured prefill remains host-sampled. The [device grammar contract](DEVICE_GRAMMAR_CONTRACT.md) lists what the model must implement. |
    88	| `supports_async_decode` | `False` | Declares split decode submission/readback and the resident-input behavior specified by `DECODE_RELOAD_CONTRACT.md`. The platform warns and disables requested async scheduling when this declaration is false. `TTAsyncDecodeController.plan_decode_reload` also reads this declaration when deciding whether ordinary device-sampled traced decode may reuse resident inputs. |
    89	| `supports_async_spec_decode` | `False` | Declares that `read_decode_output` can read a wide speculative verify and preserve the verify hidden handle until proposal. If async scheduling remains enabled with `speculative_config`, the platform rejects a model without this declaration. `supports_async_decode=True` alone does not satisfy this requirement. |
    90	| `supports_compact_host_logits` | `False` | Permits `process_decode_output_host(..., sample_rows=...)` to return only selected lane-DP host-sampling rows in the supplied order. Active or custom logits processors can require full-slot output instead. |
    91	| `supports_selective_host_readback` | `False` | Permits `read_decode_output(..., async_read=True, sample_rows=...)` to read only selected lane-DP host-sampling rows. The adapter must also declare `supports_compact_host_logits` and retain an output handle for host processing. |
    92	
    93	The [selective-read contract](DECODE_RELOAD_CONTRACT.md#host-sampling-output-and-selective-reads)
    94	defines buffer ownership, row ordering, and output shapes for both host-output
    95	capabilities. Neither host-output capability changes decode input reloads.
    96	
    97	The async capability combination has a specific order: the platform first
    98	disables async scheduling for a model without `supports_async_decode`; the
    99	platform then checks `supports_async_spec_decode` only if speculative decoding
   100	and async scheduling are both enabled. Neither declaration forces async
   101	scheduling to remain enabled when an upstream executor or launch restriction
   102	requires synchronous execution.
   103	
   104	Device sampling also falls back to the host for supported host-only sampling
   105	controls, structured output without an eligible `supports_device_grammar`
   106	decode, and unsupported logprob requests. These runtime
   107	restrictions remain in force when `supports_sample_on_device=True`. Generic
   108	speculative request restrictions remain separate from ordinary sampling: a
   109	model whose `spec_plan` offers only `argmax_ids` speculates for greedy
   110	requests only and refuses logprobs, structured output and token filters on a
   111	speculating launch, while a model that also offers `logits` speculates for
   112	sampled requests and applies all of those on the host. See
   113	[SPEC_DECODE_CONTRACT.md](SPEC_DECODE_CONTRACT.md).
   114	
   115	Sources: [platform.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/platform.py),
   116	[model_runner.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/model_runner.py),
   117	[async_decode.py](../src/vllm_tt_plugin/async_decode.py), and
   118	[DECODE_RELOAD_CONTRACT.md](DECODE_RELOAD_CONTRACT.md).
